**Key findings for the campaign:**
1. **The family is cost-dead by an order of magnitude**: 30%/yr cost hurdle vs ~12%/yr raw premium. Even the best year ever (2021: 8.5bp/d gross) < daily cost. Per charter, the negative result is the deliverable.
2. **Lookahead trap of the round**: an unshifted trailing-mean-of-ON signal scores SR 1.34 vs 0.08 honest — ON_t sits inside its own signal window. Same family as r2b's EIA publication-lag catch; generalizes to any signal whose window overlaps the booked return.
3. corr-to-champion = 0.001 — the orthogonality promise was real, but there's no net return to diversify.
4. If costs ever fall to ~1bp/side, **intraday** books (not overnight) become viable first.

